{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:13-8","provision":"BCO 13-8","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"13-8","title":"Section 13-8","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/13-8/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/13-8","current_text":{"html":"<p>The Presbytery, before receiving into its membership any church, shall designate a commission to meet with the church's ruling elders to make certain that the elders understand and can sincerely adopt the doctrines and polity of the Presbyterian Church in America as contained in its Constitution. In the presence of the commission, the ruling elders shall be required to answer affirmatively the questions required of officers at their ordination.</p>","text":"The Presbytery, before receiving into its membership any church, shall designate a commission to meet with the church's ruling elders to make certain that the elders understand and can sincerely adopt the doctrines and polity of the Presbyterian Church in America as contained in its Constitution. In the presence of the commission, the ruling elders shall be required to answer affirmatively the questions required of officers at their ordination."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"94a0b54eec213ad53deb08f9fe4e387f46d90e3373f4cd38647b018d7b192c88","parent_id":"bco:13","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_record