-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":275},"excerpt":"If BCO 13-8 is the only constitutional provision that applies to an OPC church joining the PCA, it would contradict my understanding of the jurisdictional question. But I don't believe BCO 13-8 is the only paragraph that applies. BCO Chapter 5 also applies…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"},{"id":"bco:13-8--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md:occ-c4fd501d9b8a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":275},"excerpt":"…my understanding of the jurisdictional question. But I don't believe BCO 13-8 is the only paragraph that applies. BCO Chapter 5 also applies regarding the congregation members. The provisions in BCO 5 were adopted after BCO 13-8. So, it's…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"},{"id":"bco:13-8--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md:occ-d35c77dd25a4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":275},"excerpt":"…regarding the congregation members. The provisions in BCO 5 were adopted after BCO 13-8. So, it's reasonable to","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"},{"id":"bco:13-8--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md:occ-a2846bb090e8","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":291},"excerpt":"…5 came in 2017 with a revision to 5-3. Thus, it is difficult to argue that BCO 13-8 supersedes or stands in place of the lengthy procedures of BCO 5-9, when BCO 5-9 was revised seven years after BCO 13-8. The extensive section on “The Organization of a…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"},{"id":"bco:13-8--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md:occ-caa02f27f610","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":291},"excerpt":"…history. In 1977, Mid-Atlantic Presbytery filed Overture 33 seeking to add BCO 13-8, which was enacted a year later by the 6th GA. Six years later, BCO 5-1 through 5-7 were added and enacted by the 12th GA in 1984. In 1985, BCO 5-9 was extensively…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["church transfer between denominations","OPC to PCA membership transfer","excommunication","jurisdiction","membership vows","failure to attend worship","session authority limits"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2020-6"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A church member appealed Presbytery’s affirmance of his conviction and excommunication for failing to heed Session admonition and membership vows, including prolonged absence from that church. The SJC affirmed and denied the appeal, holding that all four specifications—lack of reasonable indulgence, haste, prejudice, and injustice—were nonspeci